{
  "id": 22,
  "name": "cluster_regret_v1",
  "intent": "Introduce cluster_density as a positive reward and spread as a mild penalty so candidates sitting inside dense, uniformly-close neighborhoods of unvisited nodes rise in priority. Slightly temper the regret and return coefficients (vs. parent) to give the cluster signal meaningful influence without abandoning lookahead. Hypothesis: clustered instances benefit from staying compact within a cluster before bridging; grid stays competitive via remaining regret/return terms; uniform loses some lookahead weight but cluster_density remains near-uniform and behaves like a constant offset.",
  "tags": [
    "cluster",
    "regret"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    d = f[\"distance\"]\n    r = f[\"return_distance\"]\n    g = f[\"regret\"]\n    p = f[\"progress\"]\n    cd = f[\"cluster_density\"]\n    sp = f[\"spread\"]\n    return -d + (0.15 + 0.35 * p) * r + (0.30 - 0.20 * p) * g + 0.20 * cd - 0.05 * sp",
  "source": "live_llm",
